      "id": 234571,
      "name": "der andere Jan",
      "username": "der_andere_Jan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-12-25T00:07:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Environments represent the situation a scene occurs in - so it seems natural that those are very specific to the story they are built for.</p>\n<p>The core rules have a few select examples of environments, but give a whole chapter of building-blocks to create your own. Put simply,&nbsp;you want to have a good handfull of&nbsp;Twists and Threats of various sizes up your sleeve, and unleash them one by one&nbsp;on the environment turn.</p>\n<p>I thought about sharing one or two I made up, but ultimately decided they make little to no&nbsp;sense outside of their story.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:42.016Z",
